{# A menu: a list of links, down the side or across the top.

   `menu(items, …)` emits

     <ul class="menu w-full">
       <li>
         <a class="{RING}" href="…">Posts</a>
         <ul>
           <li><a class="{RING} menu-active" href="…" aria-current="page">All posts</a></li>
         </ul>
       </li>
     </ul>

   Each item is `{ label, url, current, open, children }`, as
   `src/admin/menu.ts` builds it: `current` marks the screen being looked at
   with `menu-active` and `aria-current`, and an item's `children` are listed
   only while it is `open`. Labels are escaped. No `<nav>` is emitted; the
   screen wraps the menu in one where it is a landmark.

   `{RING}` is the focus ring: every link is outlined in the theme's text
   colour while it has keyboard focus, because DaisyUI's menu swaps the
   outline for a faint tint and gives the current item none at all.

   Modifiers:

     direction  vertical (the default, filling its column), horizontal, or
                responsive (down on a phone, across from `lg` up)
     size       xs, sm, md, lg, xl

   A value outside its set is a render error. #}

{% set DIRECTIONS = {
  vertical: 'w-full',
  horizontal: 'menu-horizontal',
  responsive: 'menu-vertical lg:menu-horizontal'
} %}
{% set SIZES = { xs: 'menu-xs', sm: 'menu-sm', md: 'menu-md', lg: 'menu-lg', xl: 'menu-xl' } %}

{% macro _items(items) -%}
{% for item in items %}
<li>
  <a class="focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-solid focus-visible:outline-base-content{% if item.current %} menu-active{% endif %}" href="{{ item.url }}"{% if item.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ item.label }}</a>
  {% if item.open and item.children.length %}
  <ul>{{ _items(item.children) }}</ul>
  {% endif %}
</li>
{% endfor %}
{%- endmacro %}

{% macro menu(items, direction='vertical', size=none) -%}
<ul class="menu{{ DIRECTIONS | modifier(direction) }}{{ SIZES | modifier(size) }}">{{ _items(items) }}</ul>
{%- endmacro %}
